    "title": "Sharpsburg nonprofit to renovate historic 1900s-era hotel for affordable apartments - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Tawnya Panizzi ,\n1 days ago A Sharpsburg social services group that has worked for 12 years to bridge racial and economic divides is now ensuring people can afford to put down roots in the borough. Roots of Faith, which opened in 2014 as an outreach of Faith United Methodist Church in Fox Chapel, purchased the three-story brick building at 800 Main St. where it has been offering free weekly meals, health screenings and more. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 3",
